From e558e764f4bde4a895fe384232d36dcec889fec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:31:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] profile: keep the pending call when an external profile's
 socket closes

0002-Send-disconnect-signal-on-remote-device-disconnect.patch makes
ext_io_disconnected() call send_disconn_req(), which stores a new
RequestDisconnection call in conn->pending. When the socket closes
while a call to the profile owner is still pending, that call is
replaced, ext_io_destroy() cancels only the new one and frees conn,
and the reply to the first call later runs disconn_reply() (or
new_conn_reply()) on the freed conn.

That is what happens on an HFP disconnect on a LuneOS phone. The
SIL's DisconnectProfile on the headset's hands-free UUID, or a device
Disconnect, reaches ext_disconnect_dev(), which sends
RequestDisconnection to oFono's hfp_ag profile and sets conn->pending.
oFono's handler calls shutdown(fd, SHUT_RDWR) on the RFCOMM socket
before it replies, so bluetoothd sees the hangup first:
ext_io_disconnected() replaces conn->pending and frees conn, and
oFono's reply then crashes bluetoothd with SIGSEGV in disconn_reply().
On a mindphone with a Nuraphone connected over A2DP and HFP, an
hfp/disconnect through com.webos.service.bluetooth2 killed bluetoothd,
and so did a disconnect from Settings; the restarted bluetoothd also
lost oFono's audio gateway registration.
Disconnects with HFP down did not crash.

Only tell the owner when it accepted the connection and no call to it
is pending. A pending RequestDisconnection means the owner is already
dropping the connection, and ext_io_destroy() cancels that call so its
reply no longer reaches the freed conn. A pending NewConnection, or a
connection still authorizing or resolving, was never the owner's.

Upstream BlueZ does not call send_disconn_req() from
ext_io_disconnected(), so it does not have this bug.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 src/profile.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/profile.c b/src/profile.c
index 120b1d2..8da2ad1 100644
--- a/src/profile.c
+++ b/src/profile.c
@@ -908,7 +908,17 @@ drop:
 			btd_service_disconnecting_complete(conn->service, 0);
 	}
 
-	send_disconn_req(ext, conn);
+	/*
+	 * Tell the owner its connection is gone, unless a call to the owner
+	 * is still pending for it. That call's reply handler takes conn as
+	 * user data, and conn is freed below: ext_io_destroy() cancels only
+	 * the call conn->pending points at, so it must stay that call. A
+	 * pending RequestDisconnection means the owner is already dropping
+	 * the connection; a pending NewConnection means the owner never
+	 * took it, and neither did one not yet connected.
+	 */
+	if (conn->connected && !conn->pending)
+		send_disconn_req(ext, conn);
 
 	ext->conns = g_slist_remove(ext->conns, conn);
 	ext_io_destroy(conn);
